I thank the authors for their detailed response;

Extra thought regarding the Instructor schemas: I see your point, and I agree that what you are currently doing is probably the best solution in practice. I have some lingering doubts that *even if* the output formats may contain complex, nested parameter configurations, the fact that output configurations are still "forced" onto the model's answers means that we are limiting their expressiveness. Good designs are sometimes designs that go a little bit outside the box, if the box is wrong: capturing how often this happens would be really interesting, but again, likely impractical for such a benchmark. It might be a nice thing to note for "future works".

Everything else looks good to me, thanks again.

